lessons:
  id: L136
  rule: "Diátaxis + Mermaid + Premium landing = Premium Elite docs"
  source: 2026-06-11 W9 (Premium Documentation overhaul)
  detail: |
    Premium Elite documentation requires: (1) 4-quadrant Diátaxis structure
    (Tutorials, How-To, Reference, Explanation) plus 6-8 supplementary
    sections (Architecture, Operations, ADRs, Premium, Plugins, Diagrams,
    Showcase, Roadmap, Comparison, Glossary, FAQ, API Stability); (2)
    landing pages for every section; (3) Mermaid diagrams for visual
    learners; (4) MADR-format ADRs; (5) plugin-system-specific docs
    (Author/Consumer/C-ABI Spec/rustdoc); (6) per-crate READMEs (both
    public and internal); (7) citation files (CFF + CodeMeta); (8)
    cross-references as absolute GitHub URLs when files are outside
    docs/ directory.

  id: L137
  rule: "mkdocs --strict requires internal index.md for every nav section"
  source: 2026-06-11 W9 mkdocs validation
  detail: |
    When adding a new nav section to mkdocs.yml, ALWAYS create an
    index.md in that directory. Otherwise mkdocs --strict fails with
    "Doc file X contains a link 'Y/index.md', but the target is not
    found". For the W9 wave, we needed to create how-to/index.md and
    tutorials/index.md to fix missing landing pages.

  id: L138
  rule: "Files outside docs/ require absolute GitHub URLs, not relative"
  source: 2026-06-11 W9 mkdocs validation
  detail: |
    mkdocs only tracks files in the docs/ directory for link validation.
    Files at the package root (CHANGELOG.md, README.md, LICENSE, etc.)
    cannot be referenced via relative paths (../CHANGELOG.md). Use
    absolute GitHub URLs instead: https://github.com/org/repo/blob/main/path/CHANGELOG.md.
    Same for directories (../benches/ → GitHub tree URL).

do_not_ship:
  - "composite_health_0.6125 — Upstream touring hypergraph limitation, not a doc issue"
  - "1 dead_code in kazuba-plugin-ocr — Already fixed in cross-audit (L134)"
  - "10 allow(dead_code) in non-target crates — Pre-existing tech debt, defer to v3.2.0"
  - "175 pre-existing kazuba-rlm warnings — Documented, unrelated to docs"

